{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Braiding.SkeinNormalisation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Braiding.SkeinNormalisation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexCouplingNormalisation"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SkeinNormalisation.twoQ_add_two_bar_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SkeinNormalisation.twoQ_add_two_bar_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/SkeinNormalisation.lean#L147-L154","doc":"The bridge-squared ratio `[2]_q + 2` is **bar-even**, so a bar-parity\nargument cannot tell the two conventions apart: the factor between them\ncarries no sign under `q ↦ q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SkeinNormalisation.sJ_bar_antiinvariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SkeinNormalisation.sJ_bar_antiinvariant","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/SkeinNormalisation.lean#L140-L145","doc":"The (J) bridge itself is **bar-odd**: `s(u⁻¹) = −s(u)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SkeinNormalisation.barEven_bar_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SkeinNormalisation.barEven_bar_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/SkeinNormalisation.lean#L132-L138","doc":"The cofactor between the bridges is **bar-even**: invariant under\n`u ↦ u⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SkeinNormalisation.hOneSq_eq_sSq_mul_twoQ_add_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SkeinNormalisation.hOneSq_eq_sSq_mul_twoQ_add_two","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/SkeinNormalisation.lean#L118-L128","doc":"**`h₁² = s² · ([2]_q + 2)`** — the conversion factor between the two\nconventions, at the power the decay rate actually carries.\n\n`sSq` is `s²` (`WeakVertexSubstitutionScale.sSq`), and the decay-coupling rate\ncarries it once, so converting a rate from (J) to (H) multiplies by\n`[2]_q + 2`.  That factor is `4.01089686671` at the proton pin. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SkeinNormalisation.hOneSq_eq_twoQ_sq_sub_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SkeinNormalisation.hOneSq_eq_twoQ_sq_sub_four","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/SkeinNormalisation.lean#L109-L116","doc":"**`h₁² = [2]_q² − 4`.**  The (H) bridge squared is the fundamental\nquantum dimension squared minus its classical value squared — the\nsquare-root-free form of the factorisation above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SkeinNormalisation.hOne_eq_sSqrt_mul_barEven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SkeinNormalisation.hOne_eq_sSqrt_mul_barEven","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/SkeinNormalisation.lean#L100-L107","doc":"**The (H) bridge factors through the (J) bridge.**\n`h₁(u²) = s(u) · (u + u⁻¹)`: the two Skein bridges differ by the bar-even\ncofactor `u + u⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SkeinNormalisation.no_rescaling_of_skein_weights","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SkeinNormalisation.no_rescaling_of_skein_weights","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/SkeinNormalisation.lean#L81-L96","doc":"**No rescaling of the bracket carries (H) to (J).**  (H) weights the two\ncrossings `(L₊, L₋)` as `(1, −1)`; (J) weights them `(q, −q⁻¹)`.  If a single\nconstant `c` reproduced both weights, then `q = q⁻¹` — so the conventions\nagree only at `q² = 1`, the classical point where both bridges vanish.\n\nThis is the structural content of the finding: the two relations are not two\nspellings of one relation, and no normalisation constant reconciles them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SkeinNormalisation.barEven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SkeinNormalisation.barEven","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/SkeinNormalisation.lean#L76-L77","doc":"The bar-even cofactor `u + u⁻¹` separating the two bridges. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SkeinNormalisation.sJ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SkeinNormalisation.sJ","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/SkeinNormalisation.lean#L71-L74","doc":"The **(J)** bridge `s = q^{1/2} − q^{-1/2}`, written in the square-root\nvariable `u` (so `sJ u` is `s` at `q = u²`). Stating it this way keeps the\nfile over a generic field: no `Real.sqrt`, no ordering hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SkeinNormalisation.hOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SkeinNormalisation.hOne","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/SkeinNormalisation.lean#L68-L69","doc":"The **(H)** bridge of `AGENTS.md` §7a: `h₁ = q − q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}